template_notes:
Chat template (identical for 4b/12b/27b; sha256 7de1c58e208eda46): '<bos>' then per turn '<start_of_turn>{role}
{content|trim}<end_of_turn>
' with roles user/model; generation prompt '<start_of_turn>model
'. No system role in the instruction format: the HF template folds a system message into the first user turn as '{system}

{user}'; the adapter uses sys_role=None so the framing text is prepended to the user turn explicitly (byte-identical result). BOS is emitted by the template, Adapter.encode uses add_special_tokens=False -> exactly one BOS. Decoded generations end with '<end_of_turn>' followed by '<eos>' padding (core passes pad_token_id = pad or eos and Gemma's pad id 0 is falsy); split() cuts there.
